  {
    "text": "Yes. Immoozide is described as a potent inducer of the enzyme HTX-5D, while Quorerol is cleared almost entirely by that same enzyme. Induction of HTX-5D by Immoozide would therefore increase Quorerol's metabolic clearance, reducing its plasma concentrations and potentially diminishing its therapeutic effect. Because Quorerol depends on HTX-5D for essentially all of its elimination, this is a mechanism-based interaction likely to be clinically significant, even though the exact magnitude (and Immoozide's own dependence on HTX-5D) is not stated in the provided information.\n\nMECHANISM: Immoozide potently induces HTX-5D, increasing clearance of Quorerol (reduced Quorerol exposure)\nFINAL ANSWER: YES",
